<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav August industry output rises 2.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav August industry output rises 2.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT   AUG	  JULY     AUG 1995</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	   + 2.1	 - 3.1	 N.A.</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	     + 9.7	 +15.7	 N.A.</p>
<p> index (base average 1995)  102.0	  99.9	 N.A.</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE DATA (JAN TO AUG)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	     + 4.8	 + 4.1	 N.A.</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1995)  109.5	 113.2	 N.A.</p>
<p>NOTE - August output is down by 44.5 percent against the same month in 1991. Cummulative January-August output is 47.4 percent down over the same period in 1991.</p>
<p>- Data largely exclude private sector, where manufacturing is not significant. Data cover Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Gordana Kukic, Belgrade Newsroom +381 11 222 4254</p>
